<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lhazang Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1717</span> · Also known as Lha-bzang Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lhazang Khan was the last khan of the Khoshut Khanate that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>. In 1705 he killed the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangye-gyatso">Sangye Gyatso</a> and deposed the Sixth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalai-lama">Dalai Lama</a>, Tsangyang Gyatso, who died on the way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, making many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetans">Tibetans</a> hostile to him. In 1717 the Dzungar Khanate invaded Tibet, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a> and killed him, which led to the Qing intervention of 1720.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lhazang-khan.jpg" alt="Lhazang Khan" width="300" height="284" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LhaBzangKhan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
